          "draw": 0.8,
          "at": "load balancer",
          "color": "#1e6fd9"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "front",
      "chapter": "What a load balancer is",
      "narration": "A load balancer sits in front of a group of servers. Every request reaches it first. It decides which server should answer. Think of a host at a busy restaurant, sending each guest to a free table.",
