    {
      "id": "autoscaling",
      "chapter": "Why it matters",
      "narration": "When traffic spikes, say during a big sale, more servers can be added. The load balancer starts sending them work right away. When the rush ends, the extra servers are removed. Cloud providers call this autoscaling.",
