    {
      "id": "recap",
      "chapter": "Recap",
      "narration": "A load balancer spreads visitors across many servers. It picks a server with a simple rule, like round robin or least connections. It skips servers that fail their health checks. And it lets a site grow or shrink with demand. Next time a site stays fast on a busy day, picture the host at the door.",
